yupiter documentation
=====================

Plain text, one file per topic.  Start with repository, then building
and testing.


Documents
---------

repository     Map of the tree and what each entry is for.
building       Configure, build, install, consume; flags and porting.
testing        Test programs, verification kinds, golden files, rules.
formatting     The printf engine: dialect, flow, format checking.
io             Streams, staging buffer, syscalls, assembly.
heap           Allocator: arena, layout, algorithms, safe variants.
python-binding PyO3/maturin binding against libyupiter.so.
style          Documentation style rules.


Reading order
-------------

repository -> building -> testing

Then, by task:

formatting or heap -> io -> building


Conventions
-----------

Commands run from the repository root unless stated otherwise.
Public interface and C tests are ISO C17; implementation is ISO C++23;
assembly is GAS.  The header is the contract: if a document disagrees
with include/yupiter.h, fix the document.